{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-gen-9-1","title":"Genesis 9:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 God blesses Noah and his sons, and grants them flesh for food. 4 Blood and murder are forbidden. 8 God's covenant, of which the rainbow was constituted a pledge. 18 Noah's family replenish the world. 20 Noah plants a vineyard. 21 Is drunken, and mocked by his son. 25 Curses Canaan. 26 Blesses Shem. 27 Prays for Japheth, and dies.</p>\n<p>blessed. 7; 1:22,28; 2:3; 8:17; 24:60; Ps 112:1; 128:3,4; Isa 51:2 Be. 7,19; 1:28; 8:17; 10:32</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-9-2","title":"Genesis 9:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>1:28; 2:19; 35:5; Le 26:6,22; Job 5:22,23; Ps 8:4-8; 104:20-23 Eze 34:25; Ho 2:18; Jas 3:7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-9-3","title":"Genesis 9:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>Every. Le 11:1-47; 22:8; De 12:15; 14:3-21; Ac 10:12-15; 1Ti 4:3-5 even. 1:29,30; Ps 104:14,15; Ro 14:3,14,17,20; 1Co 10:23,25,26,31 Col 2:16,21,22; 1Ti 4:3,4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-9-4","title":"Genesis 9:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>the life. Le 3:17; 7:26; 17:10-14; 19:26; De 12:16,23; 14:21; 15:23; 1Sa 14:34 Ac 15:20,25,29; 1Ti 4:4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-9-5","title":"Genesis 9:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>every. Ex 21:12,28,29 and at. 4:9,10; Le 19:16; Nu 35:31-33; De 21:1-9; Ps 9:12; Mt 23:35 brother. Ac 17:26</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-9-6","title":"Genesis 9:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>by. Ex 21:12-14; 22:2,3; Le 17:4; 24:17; Nu 35:25; 1Ki 2:5,6,28-34 Mt 26:52; Ro 13:4; Re 13:10 in. 1:26,27; 5:1; Ps 51:4; Jas 3:9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-9-7","title":"Genesis 9:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>1,19; 1:28; 8:17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-9-9","title":"Genesis 9:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>11,17; 6:18; 17:7,8; 22:17; Isa 54:9,10; Jer 31:35,36; 33:20; Ro 1:3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-9-10","title":"Genesis 9:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>15,16; 8:1; Job 38:1-41; 41:1-34; Ps 36:5,6; 145:9; Jon 4:11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-9-11","title":"Genesis 9:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>And I. 8:21,22; Isa 54:9 neither shall all. 7:21-23; 8:21,22; 2Pe 3:7,11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-9-12","title":"Genesis 9:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>17:11; Ex 12:13; 13:16; Jos 2:12; Mt 26:26-28; 1Co 11:23-25</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-9-13","title":"Genesis 9:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>Eze 1:28; Re 4:3; 10:1</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-9-15","title":"Genesis 9:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>remember. Ex 28:12; Le 26:42-45; De 7:9; 1Ki 8:23; Ne 9:32; Ps 106:45 Jer 14:21; Eze 16:60; Lu 1:72 the waters. Isa 54:8-10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-9-16","title":"Genesis 9:16","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>everlasting. 9-11; 8:21,22; 17:13,19; 2Sa 23:5; Ps 89:3,4; Isa 54:8-10; 55:3 Jer 32:40; Heb 13:20</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-9-18","title":"Genesis 9:18","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":18,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":18},"content":"<p>Shem. 23; 10:1; 1Ch 1:4 Ham. 10:1,6 Canaan. Heb. Chenaan.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-9-19","title":"Genesis 9:19","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":19,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":19},"content":"<p>These. 5:32 and of. 8:17; 10:2-32; 1Ch 1:4-28</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-9-20","title":"Genesis 9:20","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":20,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":20},"content":"<p>an husbandman. 3:18,19,23; 4:2; 5:29; Pr 10:11; 12:11; Ec 5:9; Isa 28:24-26 planted. De 20:6; 28:30; Pr 24:30; So 1:6; 1Co 9:7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-9-21","title":"Genesis 9:21","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":21,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":21},"content":"<p>and was. 6:9; 19:32-36; Pr 20:1; 23:31,32; Ec 7:20; Lu 22:3,4; Ro 13:13 1Co 10:12; Ga 5:21; Tit 2:2 and he. Hab 2:15,16; Re 3:18</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-9-22","title":"Genesis 9:22","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":22,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":22},"content":"<p>Ham. 25; 10:6,15-19; 1Ch 1:8,13-16 told. 2Sa 1:19,20; Ps 35:20,21; 40:15; 70:3; Pr 25:9; 30:17; Ob 1:12,13 Mt 18:15; 1Co 13:6; Ga 6:1</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-9-23","title":"Genesis 9:23","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":23,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":23},"content":"<p>Ex 20:12; Le 19:32; Ro 13:7; Ga 6:1; 1Ti 5:1,17,19; 1Pe 2:17; 4:8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-9-25","title":"Genesis 9:25","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":25,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":25},"content":"<p>Cursed. 22; 3:14; 4:11; 49:7; De 27:16; 28:18; Mt 25:41; Joh 8:34 a servant.The devoted nations, which God destroyed before Israel, were descended from Canaan: and so were the Phoenicians and Carthaginians, who were at length subjugated with dreadful destruction by the Greeks and Romans. The Africans, who have been bought and sold like beasts, were also his posterity.</p>\n<p>Jos 9:23,27; Jud 1:28-30; 1Ki 9:20,21; 2Ch 8:7,8; Joh 8:34</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-9-26","title":"Genesis 9:26","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":26,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":26},"content":"<p>Blessed. De 33:26; Ps 144:15; Ro 9:5 the Lord. 10:10-26; 12:1-3; Lu 3:23-36 Sem. Heb 11:16 his servant. or, servant to them. 27:37,40</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-9-27","title":"Genesis 9:27","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":27,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":27},"content":"<p>enlarge. or, persuade. Japheth.Japheth denotes enlargement, and how wonderfully have his boundaries been enlarged; for not only Europe, but Asia Minor, part of Armenia, Iberia, the whole of the vast regions of Asia north of Taurus, and probably America, fell to the share of his posterity.</p>\n<p>he shall dwell.These words may mean either that God or that Japheth shall dwell in the tents of Shem. In either sense the prophecy has been literally fulfilled.</p>\n<p>dwell. Isa 11:10; Ho 2:14; Mal 1:11; Ac 17:14; Ro 11:12; 15:12 Eph 2:13,14,19; 3:6,13; Heb 11:9,10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-9-29","title":"Genesis 9:29","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":29,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":29},"content":"<p>A.M. 2006. B.C. 1998. nine. 5:5,20,27,32; 11:11-25; Ps 90:10</p>"}]}